subproblem.statement:
Let (X, μ) and (Y, ν) be measure spaces (X, Y : Type with measurable-space structures), f : X → Y, A ⊆ X, and J : X → [0, ∞] μ⌞A-a.e. measurable. Assume the area identity: for every μ⌞A-a.e. measurable h : X → [0, ∞], the fibre sum y ↦ Σ'_{x ∈ A, f(x) = y} h(x) (an unordered sum in [0, ∞] over the subtype {x // x ∈ A ∧ f x = y}) is ν-a.e. measurable and ∫⁻_A h·J dμ = ∫⁻ Σ'_{x ∈ A, f(x) = y} h(x) dν(y). Then for every μ⌞A-a.e. strongly measurable g : X → ℝ with ∫⁻_A |g|·J dμ < ∞ (|g| as the extended norm):
(i) for ν-a.e. y the real family (g(x))_{x ∈ A, f(x) = y} is summable;
(ii) y ↦ Σ'_{x ∈ A, f(x) = y} g(x) is ν-integrable;
(iii) ∫_A g(x)·J(x).toReal dμ(x) = ∫ Σ'_{x ∈ A, f(x) = y} g(x) dν(y), where J(x).toReal is J(x) as a real number (0 if J(x) = ∞).

Assume (SNA) [the frozen statement of the uncle lemma lpf_simple_nvector_algebra]: for all P, n and v : Fin n → ℝ^P, ‖simpleNVector v‖² = det(⟨v_i, v_j⟩)_{i,j}; and for all P, n, every real n×n matrix B and τ : Fin n → ℝ^P, simpleNVector(i ↦ Σ_j B_ij τ_j) = det(B) • simpleNVector τ. Then:
(a) for every Q, n and every orthonormal family σ : Fin n → ℝ^Q, ‖simpleNVector σ‖ = 1;
(b) for every Q, n and every pair of orthonormal families σ, σ′ : Fin n → ℝ^Q with span{σ_1,…,σ_n} = span{σ′_1,…,σ′_n}, simpleNVector σ′ = simpleNVector σ or simpleNVector σ′ = −simpleNVector σ.

Let P, Q, n ∈ ℕ and V ⊆ ℝ^Q open. Let M ⊆ ℝ^P be Hⁿ-null-measurable, and let θ : ℝ^P → ℝ satisfy θ(x) > 0 and θ(x) ∈ ℕ for x ∈ M, with θ Hⁿ⌞M-a.e. measurable. Let Ξ : ℝ^P → NVector(ℝ^Q, n) be Hⁿ⌞M-a.e. strongly measurable. Let f : ℝ^P → ℝ^Q be continuous on M with f(M) ⊆ V and Hⁿ(f(Z)) = 0 for every Z ⊆ M with Hⁿ(Z) = 0. Let G_k : ℝⁿ → ℝ^Q and O_k ⊆ ℝⁿ (k ∈ ℕ) be arbitrary, and S ∈ D_n(V). Assume:
(AF) for every Hⁿ-null-measurable A ⊆ M and every Hⁿ⌞A-a.e. measurable h : ℝ^P → [0, ∞], the fibre sum y ↦ Σ'_{x ∈ A, f(x) = y} h(x) is Hⁿ-a.e. measurable on ℝ^Q, and ∫⁻_A h·‖Ξ‖ₑ dHⁿ = ∫⁻ Σ'_{x ∈ A, f(x) = y} h(x) dHⁿ(y);
(LF) ∫⁻_{M ∩ f⁻¹(K)} ofReal(θ)·‖Ξ‖ₑ dHⁿ < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ V;
(CH) for Hⁿ⌞M-a.e. x with Ξ(x) ≠ 0 there are k, w ∈ O_k with G_k(w) = f(x), and an orthonormal σ : Fin n → ℝ^Q with span(range σ) = range DG_k(w), such that Ξ(x) = ‖Ξ(x)‖ • simpleNVector σ or Ξ(x) = −(‖Ξ(x)‖ • simpleNVector σ);
(S) S(ω) = ∫_M θ(x)·Ξ(x)(ω(f(x))) dHⁿ(x) for every ω ∈ Dⁿ(V).
Then there are Y ⊆ ℝ^Q and Ψ : ℝ^Q → NVector(ℝ^Q, n) with: Y ⊆ V; Y is Hⁿ-null-measurable; Hⁿ(Y ∩ K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ V; Ψ is Hⁿ⌞Y-a.e. strongly measurable; y ↦ ‖Ψ(y)‖ is Hⁿ-integrable on Y ∩ K for every compact K ⊆ V; for Hⁿ⌞Y-a.e. y, there are m ∈ ℕ, integers a_1,…,a_m, indices k_1,…,k_m ∈ ℕ, points w_i ∈ O_{k_i} with G_{k_i}(w_i) = y, and orthonormal σ_i : Fin n → ℝ^Q with span(range σ_i) = range DG_{k_i}(w_i) (i = 1,…,m), such that Ψ(y) = Σ_i a_i • simpleNVector σ_i; and S(ω) = ∫_Y Ψ(y)(ω(y)) dHⁿ(y) for every ω ∈ Dⁿ(V).

Assume (SNA) [the frozen statement of the uncle lemma lpf_simple_nvector_algebra]: for all P, n and v : Fin n → ℝ^P, ‖simpleNVector v‖² = det(⟨v_i, v_j⟩)_{i,j}; and for all P, n, every real n×n matrix B and τ : Fin n → ℝ^P, simpleNVector(i ↦ Σ_j B_ij τ_j) = det(B) • simpleNVector τ. Let P, Q, n ∈ ℕ, τ : Fin n → ℝ^P orthonormal, A : ℝ^P → ℝ^Q continuous linear, and w an n-vector on ℝ^P with w = simpleNVector τ or w = −simpleNVector τ. If A_#w := nVectorPushforward n A w ≠ 0, then:
(i) the family (Aτ_1,…,Aτ_n) is linearly independent;
(ii) there is an orthonormal σ : Fin n → ℝ^Q with span(range σ) = span{Aτ_1,…,Aτ_n} and either A_#w = ‖A_#w‖ • simpleNVector σ or A_#w = −(‖A_#w‖ • simpleNVector σ).
